<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Kerr-McGee lowered.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Kerr-McGee lowered.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Goldman Sachs analyst Donald Textor downgraded Kerr-McGee Corp market perform from market outperform, his office said.</p>
<p>-- cut 1997 earnings per share estimate to $3.80 from $4.00 and lowered 1998 view to $4.50 from $5.25.</p>
<p>-- on Thursday Kerr-McGee said lower second-quarter earnings reflected weaker operating income in all three of its business units -- exploration and production, chemicals and coal. The company reported operating earnings of $0.66 per share, versus $0.91 a share in the year-earlier period.</p>
<p>-- the stock was off 1-11/16 to 63-3/8.</p>
